data.content:
## Breaking Changes in Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0

The package upgraded from **OpenAPI.NET v1** to **OpenAPI.NET v2**, which adopted OpenAPI 3.1 / JSON Schema semantics. Here's what broke and how to fix each piece:

---

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` — removed entirely

Primitive wrapper types (`OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc.) are gone. Use `System.Text.Json.Nodes` instead:

```csharp
// Before
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

---

### 2. `Nullable` property — removed

OpenAPI 3.1 expresses nullability via a type array. `Schema.Type` is now a `JsonSchemaType` flags enum:

```csharp
// Before
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

---

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` — no longer a `Dictionary` subclass

It's now a plain class with a `Schemes` property:

```csharp
// Before
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// After
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new()
    {
        Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
        {
            [oAuthScheme] = scopes
        }
    }
};
```

---

### 4. `OpenApiReference.Type` — enum values renamed

`ReferenceType` values were renamed to match the OpenAPI 3.1 spec:

```csharp
// Before
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }

// After
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
// This one actually kept its name — but if you used others like
// ReferenceType.Schema, it's now ReferenceType.Schema (unchanged).
// Just verify your specific enum values still compile.
```

---

### Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of changes:**
| Old (v1) | New (v2) |
|----------|----------|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.*` primitives | `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonValue/JsonNode` |
| `schema.Nullable = bool` | `schema.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `new OpenApiSecurityRequirement { [scheme] = scopes }` | `new OpenApiSecurityRequirement { Schemes = { ... } }` |
